program loop_while

? `loop while COND do` is the one condition-loop form: it runs while the
? condition holds. Counter form `loop i:0 while COND do` counts from 0 while
? the condition holds.

@ main ||:
	n: 0
	loop while n < 3 do
		print|n|
		n = n + 1
	$
	m: 10
	loop while m > 8 do
		print|m|
		m = m - 1
	$
	loop i:0 while i < 2 do
		print|i|
	$
	print|["0", "1", "2", "10", "9", "0", "1"]|
$
